//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_I6AN4_SWITCH12", overlay = false)

// I6a-N4 (2026-11-07), capture row I6A-N4-2: `docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-07-i6a-n4.md`.
// The question is whether TradingView COMPILES this file. Ours SERVES it, unchanged by I6a-N4 (indent 12 is a multiple of four, two levels under the arm at 4). COMPILES and N01 equals the CONTROL = our serve is right. COMPILE FAILS = an over-serve for a later lane.
// Record isFailed() and, if it fails, status().errorDescription.editorError (code, message,
// line, column): that text IS the measurement. Paste each file ALONE (a Pine script compiles
// as a whole, so one invalid shape would hide the others).
// Indents are SPACES, counted exactly; do not let the editor re-indent on paste.

m = bar_index % 2
k = bar_index % 3
v = switch m
    0 => switch k
            0 => close
            => low
    => high
plot(v, "N01_nested_at_12")
